In this folder, some data corresponding to the ground state of ethylene, water and formaldehyde are provided.
In each folder, you can find as printouts, the orbital coefficeints, the overlap (in AO), the state density in AOs and MOs.
Furthermore, the output from the CASSCF calculation in CFOUR is given, as well as its input geometry (ZMAT file). 

The data_cfour.bin provides the necessary information on the states and can be read by the routine in read_info.py, which uses the routine written in read_cfour.py:

this gives
[n_int, n_act, n_ext]: number of internal, active and external orbitals
[n_a, n_b]: number of alfa and beta spin electrons
 ene:energy of the state
 c, C,: the c, C coefficeints associated to the CASSCF state
 S: overlap matrix
 rdm1: 1-el density matrix
 [g_ci, g_k]: Casscf gradient (CI part and orbital rotation part)
 [diag_ci, (diag_k_AI, diag_k_EI, diag_k_EA)]
 [Hx_ci, Hx_k]:Hessian-vector prodicts, Ci and orbital parts
 spin:
 mult: multiplicity

All calculations are done without point group symmetry


------------------------------------------------------
In the folder water_block2, there are the calculations done with DMRG-CASSCF in a state averaged approach.
The input file contains the geometry and the indication of the targeted spin states
the output file contains the converged energies and the associated density matriced (the orbital occupation numbers).
All calculations have been done without point-group symmetry

------------------------------------------------------
In the folder water_nakatani_tda, tda_water_julia.jl reproduces the DMRG-TDA column of Table IV of Nakatani, Wouters,
Van Neck & Chan, J. Chem. Phys. 140, 024108 (2014) with QNTensorTrains: water/cc-pVDZ, O 1s frozen (8 electrons in 23
orbitals), the lowest singlets of each C2v irrep at bond dimension M = 500, checked against per-irrep FCI (fci_vdz.txt).
Per irrep: an in-irrep MALS ramp and sweeps at the cap, a typed Riemannian CG polish of the reference to |grad| <= 1e-8,
then the TDA inside the irrep. FCIDUMP (Fiedler order) and fci_vdz.txt are regenerated by make_fcidump_fci.py and
fiedler_reorder.py (pyscf).
It needs QNTensorTrains main (>= 64182ca) as a sibling checkout of DMRG_exc_states (or set QNTENSORTRAINS_PATH):
  ./run_tda.sh                 (all four irreps at M = 500, one after the other; ./run_tda.sh 500 A1 for one)
writes logs/julia_m500_<irrep>.log and states/<irrep>.jls, then runs summarize_tda.jl, which collects the logs into
Table IV: E - E_FCI, the paper's TDA error, and the difference to the recorded run in reference_logs/.
The recorded run (QNTensorTrains 64182ca, 32 threads, AMD EPYC 9454) took 2.4-3.8 h and 17-21 GB peak memory per irrep,
with about 2.5 cores busy on average, so a workstation with ~24 GB free is enough; fewer threads should cost somewhat
more time (not measured end to end). The recorded M = 500 errors are 0.008-0.017 mHa for the references and
0.035-1.58 mHa for the excited states (paper: 0.01-0.02 and 0.04-2.69 mHa).

------------------------------------------------------
The same calculations with QNTensorTrains-rs, the public Rust library (https://github.com/paulcazeaux/QNTensorTrains-rs, Julia
bindings QNTT). Setup: clone it as a sibling of DMRG_exc_states (or set QNTT_RS_PATH) and build the C library once with
  cargo build --release -p qntt-capi          (inside the checkout; QNTT_LIB overrides the library file)
The library sizes its own thread pool: QNTT_THREADS (default all cores; Julia's -t does not apply).
  water_block2/sa_dmrg_rs.jl         the state-average notebook as a script (SSS on the SU(2) layer, STS at S_z = 0),
                                       with the block2 comparison (energies, occupations, STS 1-RDMs) and the dense FCI
                                       check; QNTensorTrains-rs 0.1.0 or later, a few seconds. All six roots agree with FCI to 1e-13.
  water_nakatani_tda/tda_water_rs.jl the DMRG-TDA reproduction of Table IV (QNTT.tda, needs QNTensorTrains-rs >= 0.1.1);
                                       ./run_tda_rs.sh [M] [irreps] runs it one irrep at a time into logs/rs_m<M>_*.log
                                       and summarizes them with summarize_tda.jl. Checked against its own Rust driver
                                       at M = 25 (A1): reference and TDA roots agree to 1e-9. No M = 500 run yet.
  water_nakatani_tda/gad_water_rs.jl GAD pinned to each irrep (QNTT.saddle_seed + QNTT.gad), the counterpart of
                                       run_gad.sh with the Rust step controller only (see its header); QNTensorTrains-rs 0.1.0 or later.
  water_nakatani_tda/reference_rs.jl the per-irrep SU(2) reference shared by the last two (aufbau CSF -> MALS ramp ->
                                       MALS at the cap M -> Riemannian CG polish).
